# Labelled claims for measuring the verifier on its own - see src/policyverify/claimset.py.
#
# One JSON object per line. Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Every claim was written against the indexed text of the section it cites and
# checked by reading that text. "verbatim" claims are sentences copied from the
# section, so they are true by construction.
#
#   label  supported | not_supported     - does the cited section support it?
#   kind   paraphrase verbatim           - supported claims
#          number role negation entity   - the section conflicts with the claim
#          unsupported wrong_section     - the section is silent on the claim
#   split  tuning | heldout              - adjust thresholds on tuning only;
#                                          report final numbers on heldout
#
# The split alternates within each kind, so both halves cover every kind.
# Created 2026-11-15 from the claims used in the project audit. All of them
# have been scored once already, so neither half is untouched; add new claims
# to the heldout half before quoting a final number.


